1
00:00:03,350 --> 00:00:06,234
This is a real run of XORR's workflow with

2
00:00:06,264 --> 00:00:08,231
the CRE command line:

3
00:00:08,261 --> 00:00:11,366
cre workflow simulate, broadcasting to Monad

4
00:00:11,396 --> 00:00:12,494
testnet.

5
00:00:12,524 --> 00:00:15,791
It reads MON from Perpl, Kuru and Chainlink,

6
00:00:15,821 --> 00:00:18,380
checks how far apart they are and the gap to

7
00:00:18,410 --> 00:00:21,027
Chainlink, and writes one report, with a

8
00:00:21,057 --> 00:00:23,830
halt flag, to XorrPriceReceiver.

9
00:00:24,330 --> 00:00:27,063
Here's that report on Monad testnet, through

10
00:00:27,093 --> 00:00:29,785
CRE's forwarder into the receiver.

11
00:00:30,285 --> 00:00:32,484
The council's Price desk reads this

12
00:00:32,514 --> 00:00:35,131
receiver. When the report is stale or

13
00:00:35,161 --> 00:00:38,359
halted, the desk vetoes, so nothing trades

14
00:00:38,389 --> 00:00:40,906
on a price the workflow didn't vouch for.

15
00:00:41,245 --> 00:00:43,281
The workflow isn't deployed on a schedule

16
00:00:43,311 --> 00:00:46,978
yet, so runs like this one keep it fresh.

17
00:00:47,478 --> 00:00:50,339
XORR, with Chainlink CRE.

